_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible 4.4 dev7, 4.3 Stable, 4.22 Stable, 4.0.1 Stable\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.4.dev7 - Windows 10 (build 19045) - Multi-window, 2 monitors - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 2070 SUPER (NVIDIA; 31.0.15.5186) - Intel(R) Core(TM) i7-6700K CPU @ 4.00GHz (8 threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nNew instances created from the same scene are referencing the same exported arrays that are modified from Editor (showing reset value).\nIf exported array isn't modified it isn't shared.\nSeems like the array is bound to a loaded PackedScene instead of actual instance of the scene.\nInstances always should get unique array variables.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- create a scene with any type node and script\n- export an Array[Type]\n- modify value from editor (shows reset button next to a value)\n- add code that manipulates that array\n- create a script in main scene that creates instances of this scene, and deletes them before creating a new instance\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[new_instance_exported_array_bug.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/18368008/new_instance_exported_array_bug.zip)\n","closed_by":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscripti